(1336466, 171278, 9906, '<td valign="top">Very nice concept!  Too bad that you appear to be blown out on the inside of the cup and just in front of it.  Also, the handle IMHO should be on the other side of the image (in the white) as it tends to dissapear into the background.  Most original I''ve seen so far though.<br/>TC</td>', 'Very nice concept!  Too bad that you appear to be blown out on the inside of the cup and just in front of it.  Also, the handle IMHO should be on the other side of the image (in the white) as it tends to dissapear into the background.  Most original I''ve seen so far though.TC', '2005-04-28 04:00:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(1336467, 171036, 36528, '<td valign="top">Very cute! IMO the image would be more effective if the duck was completely isolated - ie no evidence of the shallow bottom. A tighter crop at the top of the frame may improve this (but may have risked low marks for subject size in this particular challange).</td>', 'Very cute! IMO the image would be more effective if the duck was completely isolated - ie no evidence of the shallow bottom. A tighter crop at the top of the frame may improve this (but may have risked low marks for subject size in this particular challange).', '2005-04-28 04:01:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(1336470, 170762, 35467, '<td valign="top">Interesting photo perhaps as a sugestion the holder was to be faded out would make a striking image, Good work</td>', 'Interesting photo perhaps as a sugestion the holder was to be faded out would make a striking image, Good work', '2005-04-28 04:02:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(1336471, 171154, 9906, '<td valign="top">This is so sharp it hurts my eyes.  I think this could actually be a candidate for a soft focus effect.  It is definately the best shot I''ve seen of a dandeline that is still yellow...<br/>TC</td>', 'This is so sharp it hurts my eyes.  I think this could actually be a candidate for a soft focus effect.  It is definately the best shot I''ve seen of a dandeline that is still yellow...TC', '2005-04-28 04:02:54.000000', NULL, 1),
