(1345685, 171276, 19831, '<td valign="top">This is a nice shot. I like the tones of the photo. Excellant choice for having the boy silhouetted. Definitely fits the challenge like a glove IMO. The composition is good except...I''m wondering if it could be stronger were the boy angled "in" to the photo? The reason I say this is that, as I study the pic, I find that my attention is for sure drawn directly to your subject, the boy, but then with his stance and the pole I find my eye wanting to wander off the photo in that direction. What I''m thinking, and I could be wrong, is that if he were facing "into" the scene, that as my eye tried to follow the angle "into" the shot, I would be drawn back to the subject due to the contrasting dark silhouette. Hope that makes sense :-)  Nice job.</td>', 'This is a nice shot. I like the tones of the photo. Excellant choice for having the boy silhouetted. Definitely fits the challenge like a glove IMO. The composition is good except...I''m wondering if it could be stronger were the boy angled "in" to the photo? The reason I say this is that, as I study the pic, I find that my attention is for sure drawn directly to your subject, the boy, but then with his stance and the pole I find my eye wanting to wander off the photo in that direction. What I''m thinking, and I could be wrong, is that if he were facing "into" the scene, that as my eye tried to follow the angle "into" the shot, I would be drawn back to the subject due to the contrasting dark silhouette. Hope that makes sense :-)  Nice job.', '2005-04-30 06:05:45.000000', NULL, 1),
