(1345810, 169761, 17126, '<td valign="top">I don''t get the title (probably just don''t understand the cultural reference) but this photograph is amazing. This is the 2nd 10 I''ve given out, and like I said to the other person, the 10''s are unmistakable, you know them as soon as they pop up on the screen. This was definitely one of them. Although I do have to ask - isn''t it illegal in the open challenges to do spot desaturation? Or... is this how it looks in person? I really hope it''s legal, because I think this is a ribbon hopeful.</td>', 'I don''t get the title (probably just don''t understand the cultural reference) but this photograph is amazing. This is the 2nd 10 I''ve given out, and like I said to the other person, the 10''s are unmistakable, you know them as soon as they pop up on the screen. This was definitely one of them. Although I do have to ask - isn''t it illegal in the open challenges to do spot desaturation? Or... is this how it looks in person? I really hope it''s legal, because I think this is a ribbon hopeful.', '2005-04-30 07:40:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(1345812, 170563, 17126, '<td valign="top">I like the lighting, and the shadow it creates, but i think it would be stronger with a Jewel that was not in a setting.<br/> <br/>I was thinking that perhaps the jewel was a bright color, maybe topaz or something, then it would be more interesting as well, because the light refracted behind it would also be blue and would contrast nicely with the light colored paper. 6</td>', 'I like the lighting, and the shadow it creates, but i think it would be stronger with a Jewel that was not in a setting. I was thinking that perhaps the jewel was a bright color, maybe topaz or something, then it would be more interesting as well, because the light refracted behind it would also be blue and would contrast nicely with the light colored paper. 6', '2005-04-30 07:42:41.000000', NULL, 1),
