(1349796, 170250, 24976, '<td valign="top">great tones... i absolutely love them. If you could pm and tell me what method you used to get them I would really appreciate it. <br/>Good use of darks. i think your horizon may be slightly slanted. but very good shot overall. 9</td>', 'great tones... i absolutely love them. If you could pm and tell me what method you used to get them I would really appreciate it. Good use of darks. i think your horizon may be slightly slanted. but very good shot overall. 9', '2005-05-01 18:01:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(1349799, 170198, 29537, '<td valign="top">a too distracting shot</td>', 'a too distracting shot', '2005-05-01 18:02:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(1349802, 169000, 24183, '<td valign="top">very cute kid and a shot that you should keep in the family for a long time.  You really captured emotion and a sence of innocence.  Excellent shot,  But its not for this challenge.  Picture 10<br/>challenge 3<br/> <br/>Critique Club:  1. Lighting= Very Dim light, which people depict as gloomy ar dreery.  A high key light will depict happieness.  With a white background.  You may not want to shine bright lites on a new born baby so wait until their slightly older.<br/> <br/>2. Composition= You have captured a very nice scene, the crop could be a little tighter to the face of the baby.  The hand on the face makes the shot.  As if the baby were saying sheesh, what a crazy day.  Time to get some sleep.  <br/> <br/>3. Focus= You can get sharper photos by haveing more light so you can use a faster shutterspeed, you can also use a tri-pod to eliminate camera shake, (but you do not always have time for that) as was with this picture.<br/> <br/>Like I said before great shot, it could be sharper, but if this is your first challenge you will improve.  If you need any other advice or help with your photos, feel free to PM me.<br/> <br/>Travis</td>', 'very cute kid and a shot that you should keep in the family for a long time.  You really captured emotion and a sence of innocence.  Excellent shot,  But its not for this challenge.  Picture 10challenge 3 Critique Club:  1. Lighting= Very Dim light, which people depict as gloomy ar dreery.  A high key light will depict happieness.  With a white background.  You may not want to shine bright lites on a new born baby so wait until their slightly older. 2. Composition= You have captured a very nice scene, the crop could be a little tighter to the face of the baby.  The hand on the face makes the shot.  As if the baby were saying sheesh, what a crazy day.  Time to get some sleep.   3. Focus= You can get sharper photos by haveing more light so you can use a faster shutterspeed, you can also use a tri-pod to eliminate camera shake, (but you do not always have time for that) as was with this picture. Like I said before great shot, it could be sharper, but if this is your first challenge you will improve.  If you need any other advice or help with your photos, feel free to PM me. Travis', '2005-05-01 18:08:55.000000', NULL, 1),
