(1357429, 170846, 18552, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by jmlelii:</b></div><hr/><i> this image looks like you took this inside and shot it with a Tungsten light. Is this correct? I feel the colors are warm, perhaps a change in White balance, or a color shift is in order. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>No, not correct. This picture was taken outside just before sunset. The last rays of the sun are catching on the cattail and the water of the marsh is in dark bokeh behind.</td>', 'Originally posted by jmlelii: this image looks like you took this inside and shot it with a Tungsten light. Is this correct? I feel the colors are warm, perhaps a change in White balance, or a color shift is in order.   No, not correct. This picture was taken outside just before sunset. The last rays of the sun are catching on the cattail and the water of the marsh is in dark bokeh behind.', '2005-05-04 01:12:46.000000', NULL, 0),
