(1359166, 169486, 30049, '<td valign="top">Thanks - I could have walked up on it a bit to do that I think.  Couldn''t get any higher without some assistance as it was out in the middle of a field.<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by byoung:</b></div><hr/><i> generally i like the composition and colors a lot ... i think a slightly higher camera angle which would have placed the dark top part of the canon below the dark bottom part of the tree line would have better isolated and drawn more focus to the canon </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'Thanks - I could have walked up on it a bit to do that I think.  Couldn''t get any higher without some assistance as it was out in the middle of a field. Originally posted by byoung: generally i like the composition and colors a lot ... i think a slightly higher camera angle which would have placed the dark top part of the canon below the dark bottom part of the tree line would have better isolated and drawn more focus to the canon ', '2005-05-04 11:04:16.000000', NULL, 0),
