(1359179, 169486, 30049, '<td valign="top">You''re right.  I didn''t see that until you mentioned it.  Still learning how to use curves - obviously!  It could have been the gamma adjustment also...hmmm.  Thanks.<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by ltsimring:</b></div><hr/><i> the sky colors have some green cast, i think </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by autool:</b></div><hr/><i> Your composition is, so right, that it is almost cliche.  Nice job there.  On my monitor it has a quite green cast, even in the clouds.  If you did thid intentionally,okay, but I don''t care for it. </i></td></tr></table><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-05-04 10:07:42.</i></td>', 'You''re right.  I didn''t see that until you mentioned it.  Still learning how to use curves - obviously!  It could have been the gamma adjustment also...hmmm.  Thanks. Originally posted by ltsimring: the sky colors have some green cast, i think   Originally posted by autool: Your composition is, so right, that it is almost cliche.  Nice job there.  On my monitor it has a quite green cast, even in the clouds.  If you did thid intentionally,okay, but I don''t care for it. ', '2005-05-04 11:06:23.000000', '2005-05-04 11:07:42.000000', 0),
