(1359265, 169486, 30049, '<td valign="top">Yep, should have used a filter, although this is pretty much how it looked. It was raining (light mist) and the clouds were hanging very low with an overall light grey look to the upper ceiling.<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by hyperfocal:</b></div><hr/><i> Good composition, but the blown sky lessens the impact of the photo.  A graduated neutral density filter would have helped.  Good Work. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by bhowie:</b></div><hr/><i> Good lighting for the subject. Wish it wasn''t an open challange and you could drop the sky a few stops. If the blow out on the sky was avoided I would have given 2 points higher - I find it too distracting. Otherwise great image. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by xonkas:</b></div><hr/><i> Nice subject and composition. Too bad the sky is blown out and the cannon lacks a little contrast to the bg. Anyway, nice approach of the challenge. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by nico_blue:</b></div><hr/><i> the sky is overexposed imo. </i></td></tr></table><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-05-04 10:26:41.</i></td>', 'Yep, should have used a filter, although this is pretty much how it looked. It was raining (light mist) and the clouds were hanging very low with an overall light grey look to the upper ceiling. Originally posted by hyperfocal: Good composition, but the blown sky lessens the impact of the photo.  A graduated neutral density filter would have helped.  Good Work.   Originally posted by bhowie: Good lighting for the subject. Wish it wasn''t an open challange and you could drop the sky a few stops. If the blow out on the sky was avoided I would have given 2 points higher - I find it too distracting. Otherwise great image.   Originally posted by xonkas: Nice subject and composition. Too bad the sky is blown out and the cannon lacks a little contrast to the bg. Anyway, nice approach of the challenge.   Originally posted by nico_blue: the sky is overexposed imo. ', '2005-05-04 11:23:40.000000', '2005-05-04 11:26:41.000000', 0),
