(1360822, 170639, 21915, '<td valign="top">I had this down for a top three place. What happened ??</td>', 'I had this down for a top three place. What happened ??', '2005-05-04 18:15:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(1360829, 169847, 31133, '<td valign="top">I missed this one in the voting, but would''ve given it a high score. It''s really nice colors and the cutest damn spider ever!</td>', 'I missed this one in the voting, but would''ve given it a high score. It''s really nice colors and the cutest damn spider ever!', '2005-05-04 18:15:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(1360882, 171187, 36091, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the helpful comments!</td>', 'Thanks for all the helpful comments!', '2005-05-04 18:26:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(1360895, 171366, 21202, '<td valign="top">Your photo in or out, would have fared better in the light challenge, especially if you titled it lean forward and back.  I love your collection of lenses. Your picture of a flicker makes me hesitant to ask my question, but you asked for it so here goes:<br/> <br/>In photo shop, for color management,  for the working rgb color space, I am permitted to specify the color space of my trinitron monitor.  However, when I do save for web, it changes the color space to srgb which looks awful on my monitor.  But, if I specify the working color space as srgb, the colors do not change when I do save for web.  By the way, most all of the photos on the web look fine on my monitor and those that I edit using srgb as my working rgb color space, are not criticised     by voters but those I edit using the trinitron color space are.<br/> <br/>By the way, if you do understand color spaces, would you please comment on my entry to the surrealism challenge.<br/> <br/>Thank you very much in advance.<br/> <br/>Bill Hagerbaumer<br/>whagerbaumer@comcast.net</td>', 'Your photo in or out, would have fared better in the light challenge, especially if you titled it lean forward and back.  I love your collection of lenses. Your picture of a flicker makes me hesitant to ask my question, but you asked for it so here goes: In photo shop, for color management,  for the working rgb color space, I am permitted to specify the color space of my trinitron monitor.  However, when I do save for web, it changes the color space to srgb which looks awful on my monitor.  But, if I specify the working color space as srgb, the colors do not change when I do save for web.  By the way, most all of the photos on the web look fine on my monitor and those that I edit using srgb as my working rgb color space, are not criticised     by voters but those I edit using the trinitron color space are. By the way, if you do understand color spaces, would you please comment on my entry to the surrealism challenge. Thank you very much in advance. Bill Hagerbaumerwhagerbaumer@comcast.net', '2005-05-04 18:30:31.000000', NULL, 0),
