(1442399, 170371, 13688, '<td valign="top">The tones and soft focus in spots is incredibly soothing to me.  I''ll need to remember to come back and stare at this after a hard day of judging under-creative challenge attempts from all those who gave this under a 5.  Though there does seem to be a bit of what I assume is dust on your sensor, I don''t think it should have been a big factor in scoring in an open challenge.</td>', 'The tones and soft focus in spots is incredibly soothing to me.  I''ll need to remember to come back and stare at this after a hard day of judging under-creative challenge attempts from all those who gave this under a 5.  Though there does seem to be a bit of what I assume is dust on your sensor, I don''t think it should have been a big factor in scoring in an open challenge.', '2005-06-08 20:55:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(1447620, 170419, 37200, '<td valign="top">I think this is a really great capture.  You only get the chance at this kind of photo once or twice a year at best.  The suggestions I would have here (and I could be wrong) are the outline of the flower/stem looks to suffer from some sharpening (the hard edge).  I saw a post in the tis/tricks forum by librodo that had a link to "Luko''s sharpening".  Luko used a process that gave some definition and pop to the colors, but not the harsh edge.  May be worth playing with...  Also, and this you may have done, but not posted, I wonder what it would look like with the snow as the background for the flower.  Overall, nicely done I wish I could get a capture this good! :-)</td>', 'I think this is a really great capture.  You only get the chance at this kind of photo once or twice a year at best.  The suggestions I would have here (and I could be wrong) are the outline of the flower/stem looks to suffer from some sharpening (the hard edge).  I saw a post in the tis/tricks forum by librodo that had a link to "Luko''s sharpening".  Luko used a process that gave some definition and pop to the colors, but not the harsh edge.  May be worth playing with...  Also, and this you may have done, but not posted, I wonder what it would look like with the snow as the background for the flower.  Overall, nicely done I wish I could get a capture this good! :-)', '2005-06-11 14:06:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(1453535, 170371, 24495, '<td valign="top">Nice Curve. Nice Hug !</td>', 'Nice Curve. Nice Hug !', '2005-06-13 23:50:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(1460117, 169370, 15711, '<td valign="top">Nice simple shot. Great lighting and color!</td>', 'Nice simple shot. Great lighting and color!', '2005-06-16 10:02:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(1468468, 169605, 24983, '<td valign="top">I think the colour works against this image, Blue is a cld colour with all that it conveys, it also recedes the image into the back ground. A warm colour (red,yellow orange) jumps forward, therefore I feel if your flower had been warm with theblue background it may well have done better,</td>', 'I think the colour works against this image, Blue is a cld colour with all that it conveys, it also recedes the image into the back ground. A warm colour (red,yellow orange) jumps forward, therefore I feel if your flower had been warm with theblue background it may well have done better,', '2005-06-20 06:35:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(1471078, 171326, 15711, '<td valign="top">Simplicity at it''s finest. I love the placement of the flower. Great contrast.  Very nice!!</td>', 'Simplicity at it''s finest. I love the placement of the flower. Great contrast.  Very nice!!', '2005-06-21 12:03:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(1471470, 170762, 27373, '<td valign="top">I really like this shot, would like to see a bit more detail on the socket (being picky I guess).  But very well done, love the title.</td>', 'I really like this shot, would like to see a bit more detail on the socket (being picky I guess).  But very well done, love the title.', '2005-06-21 15:42:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(1477875, 171315, 24073, '<td valign="top">Ok, listen guys this is the thing.  I had no idea what minimilism was, I talked it over with my sister and we came up with probably Minimilism-being the bare necessities.  Having that in mind, you can ultimately see what I was aiming for here.  I know it isn''t minimilism, but at least now yall out there may see my good intentions.  TY for all the comments.  I may try to re-shoot this one in a different challenge so don''t be surprised to see it again.</td>', 'Ok, listen guys this is the thing.  I had no idea what minimilism was, I talked it over with my sister and we came up with probably Minimilism-being the bare necessities.  Having that in mind, you can ultimately see what I was aiming for here.  I know it isn''t minimilism, but at least now yall out there may see my good intentions.  TY for all the comments.  I may try to re-shoot this one in a different challenge so don''t be surprised to see it again.', '2005-06-23 10:19:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(1478242, 169839, 5792, '<td valign="top">From a technical standpoint this image is one of your best. What is great about it is that the moon is properly exposed with respect to the rest of the image and the fine detail shows up nicely.<br/> <br/>Though you don''t like them, the trees add considerable interest to the composition. The branch in the upper right isn''t really a distraction so much as it makes the image seem unbalanced without a similar branch on the upper right side. It is debatable whether or not the tiny branches should touch the moon or not. Usually it is a little more eye appealing if they do not.<br/> <br/>The sky color is a dull blue resulting from use of curves to bring out that great lunar detail. You could apply color painting on a 50% greyscale layer to bring out a deeper, darker blue that would make the moon stand out spectacularly and look great. It would also help mask the slight haloing around the branch detail. The sky is noisy and needs noise reduction applied.</td>', 'From a technical standpoint this image is one of your best. What is great about it is that the moon is properly exposed with respect to the rest of the image and the fine detail shows up nicely. Though you don''t like them, the trees add considerable interest to the composition. The branch in the upper right isn''t really a distraction so much as it makes the image seem unbalanced without a similar branch on the upper right side. It is debatable whether or not the tiny branches should touch the moon or not. Usually it is a little more eye appealing if they do not. The sky color is a dull blue resulting from use of curves to bring out that great lunar detail. You could apply color painting on a 50% greyscale layer to bring out a deeper, darker blue that would make the moon stand out spectacularly and look great. It would also help mask the slight haloing around the branch detail. The sky is noisy and needs noise reduction applied.', '2005-06-23 12:44:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(1480054, 171183, 37719, '<td valign="top">I really like the simplicity and the complexity that exist in this photo at the same time.  Simple by content maybe, complex by mood perhaps.  Very nice shot.</td>', 'I really like the simplicity and the complexity that exist in this photo at the same time.  Simple by content maybe, complex by mood perhaps.  Very nice shot.', '2005-06-24 00:22:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(1480278, 171183, 15711, '<td valign="top">Very cool. I love the lone tree in the wind.  Simplicity at its best.</td>', 'Very cool. I love the lone tree in the wind.  Simplicity at its best.', '2005-06-24 02:20:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(1480379, 171183, 21072, '<td valign="top">Great perspective, love the simplicity</td>', 'Great perspective, love the simplicity', '2005-06-24 03:39:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(1481676, 171245, 16488, '<td valign="top">I like big empty spaces in photos like this. It seems to say, what we make is insignificant, while at the same time forcing us to view the delicateness of what we (humans) make.<br/> <br/>Great sky!  A bit more drama in the light might have pleased the voters more...<br/> <br/>You may be a winner on the most 5-ish thread for those 143 votes, but you''ve also made a fine image that may be worth revisiting in post-processing sometime.</td>', 'I like big empty spaces in photos like this. It seems to say, what we make is insignificant, while at the same time forcing us to view the delicateness of what we (humans) make. Great sky!  A bit more drama in the light might have pleased the voters more... You may be a winner on the most 5-ish thread for those 143 votes, but you''ve also made a fine image that may be worth revisiting in post-processing sometime.', '2005-06-24 17:29:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(1481814, 170617, 16488, '<td valign="top">Thank you for playing the "closest to 5" game today!  With 125 5''s the voters are pushing the limits of the web page widths.  (Ok. I''ll admit I was one of those...but I don''t remember why.)<br/> <br/>What I love about photography is that it begs us to notice juxtapositions.  It entreats us to place things to complete our vision (philosophy?) of objectiveness.  If it weren''t for the "minimalism" concept of the challenge, you might have played up the contrasting textures...the sense of life and dust...the dark and the light...the grit and the softness of the petals.  I think you have a topic worth re-visiting in a future image.</td>', 'Thank you for playing the "closest to 5" game today!  With 125 5''s the voters are pushing the limits of the web page widths.  (Ok. I''ll admit I was one of those...but I don''t remember why.) What I love about photography is that it begs us to notice juxtapositions.  It entreats us to place things to complete our vision (philosophy?) of objectiveness.  If it weren''t for the "minimalism" concept of the challenge, you might have played up the contrasting textures...the sense of life and dust...the dark and the light...the grit and the softness of the petals.  I think you have a topic worth re-visiting in a future image.', '2005-06-24 18:37:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(1488814, 171343, 37779, '<td valign="top">Wow, that''s brilliant man! I love it, the contrast and the color...amazing. My eye goes to so many different things all at once, I can look at this one for a long time.</td>', 'Wow, that''s brilliant man! I love it, the contrast and the color...amazing. My eye goes to so many different things all at once, I can look at this one for a long time.', '2005-06-28 16:26:16.000000', NULL, 0),
